Derived work notice
================================================================================

The editing grammar implemented in `src/videogen/editing/` and the gate
discipline in `src/videogen/gates/` are derived from:

    Hao0321/video-autopilot-kit
    https://github.com/Hao0321/video-autopilot-kit
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Hao0321 Studio

Specifically inherited: the semantic transition table and its frequency caps,
the sub-pixel Ken Burns approach (and the permanent ban on ffmpeg `zoompan`),
the dual-mode rhythm wave, segment-index caption binding, the white-first
caption colour system, the four-layer dB ladder with sidechain ducking and
two-pass loudness normalisation, and the shared gate shell pattern.

Deliberately NOT inherited: the upstream evidence/proof layer
(`src/longform_maker/proof_stage.py`, the risky-claim regex gate, and the
"real screenshots only" rules). Upstream targets proof-driven tutorials built
from real footage; this project's source material is generative by design, so
those rules are a category error here rather than a standard being failed.

See docs/attribution.md for the per-module derivation map.

